---
import Title from "@components/global/Title.astro";
---

<section>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-8 py-12 md:px-12 lg:px-32 lg:py-32">
		<div>
			<Title title="Privacy Policy" subtitle="Last updated 5 September 2026" class="pb-10 pt-20 uppercase" />
		</div>
		<div class="prose-styles mt-12 lg:mt-24">
			<p>
				This policy explains how personal information is handled by caleb.rocks — the freelance web design service operated by
				<strong>Caleb Bruce Whittaker, sole trader (ABN 62 866 297 258)</strong>, based on the Granite Belt, Queensland, Australia ("I", "me",
				"my").
			</p>
			<p>It's deliberately short and plain, because privacy policies shouldn't need a lawyer on standby.</p>

			<h2>What information may be collected</h2>
			<p>
				If you contact me through the enquiry form, I may receive information such as your name, business name, email address, phone number and
				message. When you visit the site, hosting and third-party service providers may also process technical information such as your IP
				address, browser type, device information, request details and timestamps for purposes such as delivering the website, security and
				troubleshooting.
			</p>

			<h2>What I do with it</h2>
			<p>
				I use it to reply to your enquiry and, if we end up working together, to deliver the services you asked for. I don't sell, rent or trade
				your information, and I don't add you to any mailing list.
			</p>

			<h2>Who else sees it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>FormSubmit</strong> — processes information submitted through the enquiry form so it can be delivered to me.</li>
				<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosts this website and, like all web hosts, keeps technical server logs (such as your IP address and browser) for security and troubleshooting.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Third-party and overseas processing</h2>
			<p>
				Some service providers used by this website operate internationally or may process information using infrastructure outside Australia.
				Their handling of information is governed by their own privacy terms and applicable laws. I choose service providers with reasonable
				regard to privacy and security and only use them where reasonably necessary to operate the website or provide services.
			</p>

			<h2>Tracking and cookies</h2>
			<p>
				This website does not intentionally set first-party advertising or analytics cookies and does not currently use behavioural advertising
				or visitor-tracking analytics. Third-party services may process technical information as described above.
			</p>

			<h2>How long information is kept</h2>
			<p>
				Enquiry information is generally kept only for as long as reasonably needed to respond, manage a potential or actual client relationship,
				maintain business records, resolve disputes and meet legal or tax obligations. Information that is no longer reasonably required may be
				deleted or de-identified.
			</p>

			<h2>Access, correction and privacy concerns</h2>
			<p>
				You can contact me to ask what personal information I hold about you, request a correction, or ask for information to be deleted where
				appropriate. I aim to handle personal information responsibly and consistently with applicable Australian privacy law. If you have a
				concern, contact me first and I will try to resolve it promptly.
			</p>

			<h2>External links</h2>
			<p>This site links to a small number of external sites (if any). Their privacy practices are their own — check their policies.</p>

			<h2>Governing law</h2>
			<p>
				These terms are governed by the laws of Queensland, Australia. Subject to any rights that cannot lawfully be excluded, the parties submit
				to the courts and tribunals having jurisdiction in Queensland.
			</p>

			<h2>Severability</h2>
			<p>If any part of these terms is found to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining terms continue to apply to the extent permitted by law.</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it. Material changes will be flagged on the home page.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@caleb.rocks">hello@caleb.rocks</a>.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
